{
  "name": "1942_el_alamein",
  "title": "Second Battle of El Alamein, Oct-Nov 1942",
  "notes": "Second El Alamein, 23 Oct - 4 Nov 1942 — the NORTHERN sector fight (the Lightfoot/Supercharge corridor, coast to Miteirya). The province is the coastal El Alamein railway station area, the 8th Army's forward railhead; the Axis line lay west of the village in the Devil's Gardens minefield belt. Rosters researched (Wikipedia Second Battle of El Alamein + OOB article per Joslen/Playfair Vol. IV, de/it Wikipedia battle + OOB articles, Defence of Outpost Snipe, 9th/22nd/23rd Armoured Brigade articles, 19th Flak Division, Schneck 'Breaching the Devil's Garden'). AXES: the 8th Army assembled EAST of the line (Alexandria railhead) and attacked due west; dirs=E (coastal road/rail corridor) + SE (inland flank tracks) mirror the two Lightfoot corridors (Sun/Moon/Star north of Miteirya, Bottle/Ink/Boat/Hat against it); the Axis held the west with the 164. leichte + Italian corps in the mine belt and the panzer reserves behind. ATTACKER (84 bns): XXX Corps infantry — 51st (Highland) Div (152/153/154 Bdes: 2 & 5 Seaforth, 5 Camerons, 1 & 5/7 Gordons, 1/5/7 Black Watch, 7 A&SH; 126/127/128 Fd, 61 AT, 40 LAA; fresh from the UK, first battle), 9th Australian Div (20/24/26 Bdes: 2/13, 2/15, 2/17, 2/28, 2/32, 2/43, 2/23, 2/24, 2/48; 2/7, 2/8, 2/12 Fd, 3 AT, 4 LAA; 2/48 took Point 29 on 25/26 Oct), 2nd NZ Div (5/6 Bdes: 21/22/23/28 Maori + 24/25/26; 4/5/6 Fd, 7 AT, 14 LAA), 1st SA Div (1/2/3 Bdes, org 55 after the July fighting; 1/4/7 Fd, 1 AT, 1 LAA); X Corps armour — 1st Armd Div (2nd Armd Bde: Queen's Bays & 9th Lancers Shermans, 10th Hussars Crusaders; 7th Mot Bde: 2 KRRC, 2 & 7 Rifle Bde; 2 & 11 (HAC) RHA, 76 AT, 42 LAA), 10th Armd Div (8th Armd Bde: 3 RTR Grants, Sherwood Rangers Shermans, Staffs Yeo Crusaders; 24th Armd Bde: 41/45/47 RTR Shermans; 133rd Lorried Bde: 2/4/5 Royal Sussex; 1 & 104 (Essex Yeo) RHA, 84 AT, 53 LAA), 9th Armd Bde (3rd Hussars Grants, R Wilts Yeo Shermans, Warks Yeo Crusader III — the Supercharge charge, 94 tanks in, 24 out against the 88mm screen), 23rd Armd Bde (8/40/46/50 RTR Valentines, ~186 tanks, the gap-breaching tank force, crews the July Ruweisat survivors, org 55). DEFENDER (59 bns): the northern line — 164. leichte Afrika-Div (IR 125 I/II, IR 382 I/II/III — II./382 destroyed by the 51st at minefield L 25-26 Oct — IR 433 I/II; AR 220, Pz.Jg.220, Pi.220, org 55), Div. Trento Motorizzata (61/62 Rgt, 46 Art Rgt, IV Btg AT 47/32, org 50 — lost half its infantry by 26 Oct), Div. Bologna (39 Rgt 3 bns + 40 Rgt 2 bns, 205 Art Rgt, org 50), 15. Panzer-Div (Pz.Rgt.8 I/II, 119 tanks: Pz.III J/L 5cm L/42-L/60 + Pz.IV F2 7.5cm L/43; Pz.Gren.Rgt.115 I/II/III, AR 33, Pz.Jg.33 Marders, Pz.Pi.33, Aufkl.33 — the NORTHERN reserve, counterattacked the Kidney feature 24-27 Oct), Div. Littorio Corazzata (133 Carristi Rgt IV/XII/LI bns M13/40, 12 Bersaglieri Rgt XXI/XXIII/XXXVI, 3 Art Rgt Celere, XXIX 8.8cm group, org 50 — northern reserve with 15. Pz), 90. leichte Afrika-Div (Pz.Gren.Rgt.155/200/361 — the best Axis infantry, coastal reserve at El Daba, committed from 26 Oct; AR 190, Pz.Jg.190). The 19. Flak-Division's 88mm (piercing 100 — the tank-killers of the Kidney/Snipe screen) ride the 164th and 15. Pz (P2 ruling: every gun/AT/AA rides a line division). EXCLUDED (historically out of the northern sector): 21. Panzer-Div + Ariete (SOUTHERN reserve pinned by the XIII Corps feint — 21. Pz pulled north only 26/27 Oct), Ramcke Parachute Bde + Folgore + Brescia + Pavia (central/southern line), Trieste (army reserve at Fuka), 1st Army Tank Bde 42/44 RTR (never committed), 4th Indian Div (held Ruweisat south of the province), 7th Armd Div + 50th/44th Divs + Greek/Free French Bdes (XIII Corps southern sector). Player attacks (the 8th Army offensive); the AI defender plays elastic_defense (delay + counterattack — the 15. Pz/Littorio historical role). 1942 equipment calibration: Sherman M4 75mm armor 80/piercing 81, Grant 65/81 (75mm in the hull), Crusader II 2-pdr 25/55, Crusader III 6-pdr 28/75, Valentine 2-pdr 60/55, Pz.III J/L 50/70, Pz.IV F2 60/92 (besides the 88 the only gun that frontally kills a Sherman/Grant), M13/40 40/45 (hopeless vs the Grants — historical), 6-pdr AT 75, Marder/PaK 90, Italian 47/32 45, 88mm 100. Pure desert: def -15%, no cover; VP1 town = the 3-hex urban flag.",
